meta {
  name: Ask (/evidence/ask)
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/evidence/ask
  body: multipartForm
  auth: none
}

headers {
  Cookie: {{sessionCookie}}
}

script:pre-request {
  // The page this request stands in for renders from GET /patient and sends that response's contextKey;
  // without it the endpoint answers 409 (EvidenceEndpoints). An empty key fails closed.
  const axios = require("axios");
  const res = await axios.get(bru.getEnvVar("baseUrl") + "/patient", {
    headers: { Cookie: bru.getEnvVar("sessionCookie") || "" },
    validateStatus: () => true,
  });
  bru.setVar("contextKey", res.status === 200 && res.data ? res.data.contextKey || "" : "");
}

body:multipart-form {
  context: {{contextKey}}
  question: Given this patient's latest potassium and kidney function, what do the guidelines say about continuing an ACE inhibitor?
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
  res.body.answer: isString
  res.body.answer.length: gt 0
  res.body.handoffs: isArray
  res.body.handoffs.length: gte 4
  res.body.evidence: isArray
  res.body.citations: isArray
  res.body.suppressedClaimCount: isNumber
}

docs {
  UC-10 (REQUIREMENTS.md / REQUIREMENTS.md) - "evidence-grounded answer", which extends REQUIREMENTS.md's UC-2 and
  UC-3. Numbered UC-10, not UC-7: REQUIREMENTS.md's Week 2 use cases were originally UC-6/UC-7/UC-8, which
  collided with REQUIREMENTS.md's own UC-6 ("On-demand day's agenda", the Agenda/ requests below); both docs
  now use UC-9..UC-11 for the Week 2 set. See `Documents/Ingest.bru` for UC-9.

  This is the evidence path, and it is what the collection could not reach before. A single
  multipart POST runs the whole Week 2 supervisor graph (ARCHITECTURE-DOCUMENTS.md §6): evidence-retriever
  over the guideline corpus, answer-composer, then the Week 1 verifier reused as the `critic` node,
  which suppresses any claim it cannot attribute to a retrieved source.
  `METRICS.md` calls this the canonical "Week 2 core flow" a grader runs.

  IT IS NOT THE COLLECTION'S ONLY AGENT REQUEST, AND SAYING SO WOULD BE WRONG. `GET /agenda` runs
  the agent loop too: `AgendaRosterService` fans `AgendaPatientSummaryRunner` per patient, which
  calls `IAgentOrchestrator.StartAgendaSummaryAsync` - the SAME `RunTurnAsync` the chat brief uses,
  verification gate included - so `AgendaRow.Summary` is a cited summary and `AgendaRow.SafetyFlags`
  are FR-VERIF-2 constraint flags. What was missing was not agent behaviour; it was the *evidence*
  path: a question answered against the guideline corpus and the patient's document facts.

  IT IS NOT THE MULTI-TURN HALF OF UC-2. `/evidence/ask` is stateless - a fresh graph run per
  request, no conversation store - so it produces UC-2's *cited answer* but not its turn-to-turn
  context. That half lives on the SignalR chat hub, which a plain HTTP collection cannot drive (see
  the README's "What's not covered, and why").

  `question` is the only required part; `Ask With Document.bru` adds the document leg. The patient
  is taken from the session and is NOT a request field - EvidenceEndpoints.HandleAskAsync reads
  `session.PatientId` and re-checks the clinician-patient relationship on every call, so a launched
  session cannot name another patient (FR-AUTH-2's third choke point). There is
  no request field to point elsewhere, so the 403 path is not something this request can provoke:
  it fires when the *session's own* clinician-patient relationship no longer holds at call time,
  and returns a refusal body rather than data.

  WHAT THE ASSERTIONS MEAN. `handoffs.length >= 4` is the graph's own floor with no document
  attached - supervisor->evidence-retriever, supervisor->answer-composer, answer-composer->critic,
  critic->supervisor - so a short trace means a node was skipped, not that the answer was merely
  returned. `citations` is asserted as an array, not as non-empty: it carries click-to-source
  citations for *document-derived* facts, so it is legitimately empty until something has been
  ingested for this patient (`Documents/Ingest.bru`) or attached in-turn. `evidence` is the
  guideline snippets retrieved this turn.

  BOUND TO A PAGE'S PATIENT. The `context` part is the `contextKey` GET /patient returns,
  read by the pre-request script, because evidence.html sends the key of the patient its header
  shows and the endpoint answers any other key - or none - 409 instead of answering about whichever
  patient the session now holds. Both Evidence/ requests share the script, and it costs one
  GET /patient (four FHIR reads, one `patient_context` audit row) per request.

  NEEDS A SESSION, AND NEEDS WEEK 2 CONFIGURED. Without a `sessionCookie` this returns 401 before
  any retrieval or LLM work happens, so the assertions fail closed. Without
  `AgentForgeData__ConnectionString` set, the route is never mapped at all and this returns 404 -
  the same red, a different cause. The README's "Week 2 endpoints" section has both.
}
